  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "During a sealed battle-stage spar in Shang clan city, Wei Yang forms two broadswords of light and charges Fang Yuan. Fang Yuan names sword shadow Gu together with Broadsword Light Gu as the attack comes in.",
        "chapters": [
          265
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_shang_clan_city",
          "char_wei_yang",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_broadsword_light_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At a rock gambling shop, dissection masters open a living rank three sword shadow Gu for Fang Yuan. The shopkeeper says it can sell for thirty two thousand primeval stones after an eight thousand spend. Wei Yang says the Gu is at the same level as his broadsword light Gu and advises Fang Yuan to keep and use it rather than sell it. Fang Yuan treats the find as luck, not the Gu he was hunting.",
        "chapters": [
          280
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "rock-gambling-find",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "After a soul explosion kills Tu Bo, Bian Si Xuan binds Fang Yuan with surging sword-like shadows. Narration names rank four multiple sword shadow Gu as the shadows strike and spark off his turtle jade wolf skin Gu. She drives the shadows harder while sending a thin snake, then calls the multiple sword shadow Gu back and retreats as a black shadow when Fang Yuan pounds the bindings.",
        "chapters": [
          504
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "bian-si-xuan-ambush",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_tu_bo",
          "char_bian_si_xuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Bian Si Xuan already has multiple sword shadow Gu, but the attacks stay dispersed and struggle against strong defense. She wants overlapping shadow Gu so the sword shadows can stack into one heavy strike, then leaves that Gu with the alliance leader for later.",
        "chapters": [
          505
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "overlapping-shadow-plan",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
